WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.940
- Okay, I was expecting
to roast all these drinks

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.220
and be like like a snob, but like,

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.228
I haven't had a bad drink yet.

00:00:08.228 --> 00:00:11.395
(soft hip hop music)

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.123
Hi, what's up?

00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:17.430
My name is Chris and I worked

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.790
as a barista at Voltaire in San Jose.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.337
And people always ask baristas,

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:22.920
"have you ever served a celebrity?"

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.480
I haven't, but I see a lot

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.260
of people leaking celebrity orders online

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.238
and I thought I'd try to make some

00:00:28.238 --> 00:00:30.830
of them at home and see
if there are any good.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.270
I know Ariana Grande's
had that one coffee line

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.670
in that one song that was

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.270
everywhere last year.
♪ I've been drinking coffee ♪

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.710
Apparently now she's like
a Starbucks ambassador

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:40.300
and she has her own secret menu drink

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.450
called the Ariana Grande Frappuccino.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.760
Doesn't make that much sense

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.340
because she's vegan, but
it does sound really good.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.510
It's gonna start off with
a vanilla bean Frappuccino

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.440
which apparently doesn't
have coffee in it.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.040
So I'm gonna use vanilla bean ice cream

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.290
with milk and ice.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.360
And I'm gonna add in raspberry syrup.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.700
I couldn't find that syrup anywhere.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.870
So I just use raspberry preserves
and turned it into a syrup

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:02.690
on the stove by adding water
and a little bit more sugar.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.970
I'm surprised the raspberry jam

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.510
into syrup thing turned
out as well as it did.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.700
Then we got chocolate
chips, chocolate syrup

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.850
and I'm gonna mix that
in and blend it all.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.840
And obviously you've got to
serve it in a clear glass,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.540
top it with whipped cream
and a little bit of caramel.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.213
Okay. Yeah.

00:01:23.213 --> 00:01:24.520
Yeah. That's that's really good

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.490
but I don't know what else I was expecting

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.310
because it was literally
just an icy milkshake

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.823
which is always gonna be good.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.910
So it definitely would have been better

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:34.570
if I used full fat ice cream and milk.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.960
That's probably where the raspberry comes

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.810
into play because it's a little bit acidic

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:40.800
and acid generally tends
to cut through fats.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.720
That's why people use like
lemon juice, vinegar, lime,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.030
whenever they make like
really fatty meats.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.148
This is coming out of nowhere, but I feel

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:50.110
like a pinch of salt, you
know, like salted caramel.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.630
I don't know why ,that
would make it better.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.860
Now, Charli D'Amelio
recently did a partnership

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.450
with Dunkin on a drink called The Charli.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.540
I'm gonna taste test this recipe using

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.800
the actual Dunkin cold-brew packets.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.800
And I'm just gonna follow the
instructions that they give

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:03.633
on the box.

00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:04.466
I'm gonna measure out all

00:02:04.466 --> 00:02:06.780
of my water just to make
sure I'm not messing this up.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.020
I think four cups is

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.070
like 950 milliliters
or something like that.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:11.903
And I'm gonna Saran Wrap the top

00:02:11.903 --> 00:02:14.763
of my container and put it
in the fridge overnight.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.960
It's been about 12 hours
and I took the cold brew

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.960
out and made The Charli right over here.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.840
It's just cold brew with milk and caramel.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.470
I have no clue what a caramel pump is.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.400
So I just went with three tablespoons.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.610
It's supposed to be three pumps.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:32.070
So I'm gonna taste test the pure cold brew

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:32.970
on its own just

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.860
because I don't want to
do Dunkin dirty like that.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:35.693
I don't want to mess

00:02:35.693 --> 00:02:37.623
up the recipe and then like, not like it.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.020
Okay. I kind of messed up
because I got donuts last night.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.698
So my mouth is already
really clammy and sticky.

00:02:47.698 --> 00:02:50.980
So the caramel definitely
doesn't help that much.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.500
Okay. So a few things to note.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.870
One, as expected,

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:58.220
it is a super dark, really low
acidity kind of bitter roast.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.040
And that makes a lot of
sense, 'cause they probably

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.670
expect people to drink it
with milk and this kind

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.340
of a coffee bean pulls itself
up to milk really well.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.650
And it has a really
light body in the sense

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.630
that the mouth feel in
your mouth feels physically

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.000
like water, but it is super strong.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.270
I know the whole flavor notes
thing is super pretentious

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.130
but I'm not getting
anything specific in here.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.690
Maybe chocolaty, nutty kind
of stuff, no fruitiness

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:26.320
or tartness or bright
sweetness in the coffee itself.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.153
And that makes a lot of sense

00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:30.270
because they're probably trying
to appeal to as many people

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.070
as possible by using a
really balanced blend.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.290
And it tastes exactly

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.390
like you would expect
traditional coffee to taste.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.300
Like I used to think

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.930
that I would never ever drink coffee black

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.370
but that's just because I
was using really dark roasts

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.930
from large commercial brands.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.700
They really try to sell you on that saying

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.880
that it's stronger, but you
can get a stronger flavor

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.140
in lighter or medium roast just
by the way that you brew it.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.070
And dark roast tend to hide

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:57.400
inconsistencies and
imperfections in beans.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.980
But yeah, I really like this.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.480
Back to Ariana Grande, she
partnered with Starbucks

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.950
on another drink called
the Cloud Macchiato.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.300
It looks cool because it
has this really fluffy foam

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.630
that they call Cloud Foam.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.010
And I think we can replicate

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:12.010
that by using icing sugar
and powdered egg whites

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:14.120
which I got in the form
of meringue powder.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.990
I got some of the Starbucks espresso beans

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.850
but I don't have an espresso machine.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.177
So I try to make something
that's just close enough

00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:22.510
by dialing it in

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:26.000
on a Moka pot and know it's
technically not espresso.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.310
Like it doesn't have enough pressure.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.270
So you don't end up

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.640
with that crema on top, but like, come on.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.070
I tasted it before putting the milk

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.250
and and it's close enough, like, relax.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.250
I'll take it off the stove

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.960
once it starts bubbling and I'll run it

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.240
under cold water to stop the extraction.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.230
It should give me about
45 to 50 grams or so.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.530
And then I gotta make the foam.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.810
I don't have an electric mixer,

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.010
so we're gonna have to
whip this one by hand

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.400
which gives me really bad
flashbacks to Dalgona Coffee.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.490
So I brought an elbow brace
just in case of tendonitis.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.310
Yeah, whipping anything by hand takes

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.900
about like 20 years or so.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.950
It's about the journey

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.470
not the destination or
something like that.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.420
Put some milk and then get a spoon,

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.033
and make it look on nice.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:07.863
Look at that.

00:05:07.863 --> 00:05:10.340
And then they make this
waffle thing with the caramel.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.610
Here we have it right here.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.490
All of the normal size cups
were in the dishwasher,

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.550
but this is actually closer

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.680
to the traditional macchiato size.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.560
The Italian macchiato is just two shots

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.360
of espresso with a tiny little
dollop of foam milk on top.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.433
This is not the Starbucks macchiato

00:05:24.433 --> 00:05:26.270
because they do it like backwards.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:28.210
There's just like a latte macchiato

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.760
but the typical cafe macchiato

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.240
or espresso macchiato
is like barely any milk.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.520
And it's like that small.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.313
So let's go ahead and try it.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.240
Okay, I was expecting to roast all

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.130
of these drinks and be
like, like a snob, but like

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.920
I haven't had a bad drink yet

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:52.599
but the caramel on top is
actually is a caramel or caramel?

00:05:52.599 --> 00:05:55.900
The caramel, caramel. The
caramel's a nice touch.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.650
I feel like all Starbucks drinks
are kind of the same thing.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:02.080
It's just like vaguely milky coffee kind

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.560
of flavor with some hint of sweetness.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.930
Yeah. The foam barely
tastes like anything.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.610
So I tried to find other
interesting coffee orders.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.550
Everyone else just gets soy lattes.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.100
But in an interview,
Chloe Kardashians said

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.250
that she gets a venti seven
pump, no water chai latte.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.370
First of all, chai is just
tea, so it has to have water.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:23.110
Second, how is it a pump?

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.690
What I think they mean is

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.870
that they just brew chai
tea and then reduce it

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.720
down to like a concentrate
that they use as a syrup.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.190
And then when they serve
it, they just cut it

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.060
with water to make it back into
tea and then make the latte.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.070
So Chloe probably just wants
the concentrate with the milk.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.410
I saw that Starbucks on
their website shows what's

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.670
in their chai and I could
do that from scratch,

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.630
but it's kind of similar

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.480
to this teabag that I
found at the grocery store.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.990
I'm gonna use seven bags

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:50.400
and then reduce it down
into a syrup with sugar

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.930
that's roughly what seven pumps would be

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.330
in volume and then make
the latte out of that.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:56.840
Let's go ahead and try it.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.923
(soft hip hop music)

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.550
Okay. That's not bad.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.220
If I had to pick a least favorite one

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.810
it would probably be this one

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:11.450
but I'm surprised that it's pretty spicy

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.000
and it cuts through the milk pretty well.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:13.950
I learned a few things.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.490
One, you can make a
dessert taste fancier just

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.330
by adding some kind of acidic tart fruit.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.520
Even if the dessert itself isn't supposed

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.750
to be acidic or tart.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.450
I learned that cold-brew packets work.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:25.510
You can just make syrups

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:29.532
on the stove and foam is exhausting.

00:07:29.532 --> 00:07:32.865
(upbeat hip hop music)

